
uedcli/game/staging/

.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.swp
_scratch/

# Feature worktrees live here — a worktree is a full second checkout, so leaving
# it visible would let `git add` stage a duplicate tree and would double every
# ripgrep hit and pytest collection. Precise, not blanket `.claude/`, so
# settings.json stays tracked. (dev/docs/rules/worktrees.md)
.claude/worktrees/

# The working game copy `dev/scripts/install-deusex-assets.sh` assembles, plus its
# `.cache/<game>/{download,unpacked}` scratch. All COPYRIGHTED Deus Ex content and
# multi-gigabyte installer artifacts — user-supplied, never committed. Both the
# script and dev/docs/deusex-assets-setup.md state this is gitignored; until now
# nothing enforced it, so a `--url` run left `?? dev/games/` in the tracked tree.
dev/games/

# Per-machine project selection `dev/scripts/setup-game-preview.sh` writes at the repo root
# (`game = "<name>"` + local paths). Machine-local, not shared state — never committed.
/uedcli.toml
